    {
      "id": 224431,
      "name": "FearLord",
      "username": "FearLord",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/5f8ce5/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2018-11-30T11:15:28.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Good episode and sort of makes me wish Villain Team mode in the game had more proper ‘teams’ of Villains. Other than the Frightful Five, a lot of the other team villains, while interesting, don’t really feel like a coherent team.</p>\n<p>Mecha Stalin is an interesting character, and I think the only Sentinel’s character that references a real world personality directly. It obviously invites a comparison between our world and the Sentinels comics Universe - did the Cold War play out in a similar way? America seems to have a large number of super heroes, several of which are affiliated with the government- would the presence of the Freedom Five not have upset the balance of power, or is the implication that the USSR had its own super powered soldiers all along that maintained a similar deterrent effect as in our world with Missiles?</p>\n<p>We know about the original Iron Curtain a little - although have we seen any art of him?</p>",
      "post_number": 11,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:57:49.507Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
